    id: "cons-2025-hl-q2-a-safety-training", topicId: "cons-1-8", conceptId: "maintaining-a-health-and-safety-culture-safety-training",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2025 HL Q2(a)",
    questionText: "Discuss in detail the importance of any two of the following in maintaining a positive health and safety culture among workers on a construction site: safety training; health and safety officer; risk assessment audit.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 12,
    rows: [
    { id: "importance", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "The importance of any two in maintaining a positive health and safety culture", marks: 12, contextNote: "Any two of the three, 6 each, discussing why each matters to a positive health and safety culture. Safety training: Safe Pass is mandatory and kept current through refresher courses; training builds awareness of site risks and the skills to identify them and follow best practice; specialist tickets for machinery and vehicles; monitoring and enforcing safe work practices; it may be a condition of the insurance provider. Health and safety officer: provides induction and ongoing training (working at heights, machinery use); develops emergency response plans; keeps first aid and emergency equipment available; ensures the correct PPE is worn; carries out safety inspections and risk assessments; reviews the safety statement; investigates, records and reports accidents. Risk assessment audit: provides a safe working environment; evaluates compliance with safety regulations and policies; identifies hazards and puts control measures in place where a risk cannot be eliminated (for fire: alarms, evacuation signage, drills, extinguishers); recommends improvements; identifies training needs; reduces accidents and liability.", group: {"claimMax":2,"perOption":6,"options":["Safety training","Health and safety officer","Risk assessment audit"]} },
    ],
