    id: "cons-2015-hl-q9-b", topicId: "cons-6-2", conceptId: "thermal-bridge-junctions-b",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2015 HL Q9(b)",
    stem: "It is proposed to design the external envelope of a dwelling house to be thermal bridge free. The drawing shows an outline section through a two-storey house having a 450 mm external concrete block wall with a 250 mm full-fill insulated cavity. The roof is a traditional cut roof, the first floor has tongue-and-groove flooring on timber joists and the ground floor is an insulated solid concrete floor.",
    questionText: "Discuss the importance of designing a building envelope that is thermal bridge free.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 12,
    rows: [
    { id: "point-1", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Discussion (point 1) - 2 marks for point, 4 marks for discussion", marks: 6, contextNote: "Give a distinct valid point (2) and develop its importance (4). Source-supported routes include reduced heat loss and heating demand; more even internal surface temperatures and comfort; less risk of cold surfaces reaching dew point, condensation and mould; less material deterioration and associated health effects. Explain the causal relationship, not just a label, and avoid repeating the other point. Thermal bridging is local increased conduction; airtightness alone does not remove every conductive bridge.", permittedMarks: [0,2,4,6] },
    { id: "point-2", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Discussion (point 2) - 2 marks for point, 4 marks for discussion", marks: 6, contextNote: "Give a distinct valid point (2) and develop its importance (4). Source-supported routes include reduced heat loss and heating demand; more even internal surface temperatures and comfort; less risk of cold surfaces reaching dew point, condensation and mould; less material deterioration and associated health effects. Explain the causal relationship, not just a label, and avoid repeating the other point. Thermal bridging is local increased conduction; airtightness alone does not remove every conductive bridge.", permittedMarks: [0,2,4,6] },
    ],
